fied\",\"summary\":\"Export file /etc/exports.d/shared.exports created, nfs-server enabled/started, exportfs -v confirms /srv/nfs/shared exported to node2's IP with rw,root_squash. Export state also confirmed intact after node1 reboot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-ceb3654ab6774d1b\",\"cmd-b481c47f4a3a4995\",\"cmd-28299d5bcaf64f4f\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2\",\"requirement\":\"Mount the share at /mnt/shared on node2\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"mount output on node2 shows 10.100.251.10:/srv/nfs/shared mounted at /mnt/shared type nfs4, and fstab entry with _netdev added for persistence. Mount also confirmed recovered after node2 reboot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2818cb9a06534f16\",\"cmd-e217ae63838a4da8\",\"cmd-48c354a3f65f46f1\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3\",\"requirement\":\"Shared identity dataops with UID/GID 4500 created on both node1 and node2\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"id dataops confirms uid=4500(dataops) gid=4500(dataops) on both nodes.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-fc8871ebd40f4e1b\",\"cmd-61019bc2fb404f3b\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4\",\"requirement\":\"Shared directory set to dataops:dataops with mode 2770 on both export and mount point\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"ls -ld shows drwxrws---. dataops dataops on /srv/nfs/shared (node1) and /mnt/shared (node2), verified both before and after the reboot cycle.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-1bacfb4dd64b4b0b\",\"cmd-2818cb9a06534f16\",\"cmd-28299d5bcaf64f4f\",\"cmd-48c354a3f65f46f1\"]},{\"id\":\"req-5\",\"requirement\":\"Files created on either system keep consistent ownership/permissions across both sides\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"File from_node2.txt created on node2 shows dataops:dataops ownership visible from node2's own listing (as dataops user), and file from_node1.txt created on node1 (via NFS-backed same directory) also shows dataops:dataops; both files visible with consistent ownership from the node2 mount listing before cleanup. Root write attempt was correctly squashed (permission denied), consistent with root_squash export option.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-177fde8b24994bbe\",\"cmd-7546f0a05f49444a\",\"cmd-32fd43fb399d4f80\",\"cmd-6db3fa9fef1f4873\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.93,\"summary\":\"Reviewed all state-changing executor commands chronologically. User/group creation, package installs, export configuration, mount, fstab entry, and the firewalld rule additions (cmd-85af7db02a2d452f) on node1 were each a direct, necessary prerequisite for the task or a fix for an observed blocker (initial mount hung due to closed firewall ports, confirmed by the timeout in cmd-46f18df72ea24287). The firewall change was narrowly scoped to the three NFS-related services rather than broadly opening the host. All verification test files created during cross-node consistency checks (from_node2.txt, from_node1.txt) and post-restart checks (post_node1_restart.txt, final_check.txt) were subsequently removed (cmd-6db3fa9fef1f4873, cmd-befbe9ce74e94349, cmd-989c4f27b7be4a31), leaving no residue, and the after-executor lifecycle snapshot shows no unexpected failed services or damaged package state on either node. No unnecessary or unreverted mutations were identified.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-85af7db02a2d452f\",\"cmd-46f18df72ea24287\",\"cmd-6db3fa9fef1f4873\",\"cmd-befbe9ce74e94349\",\"cmd-989c4f27b7be4a31\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node2:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\",\"global:after_executor:node2:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence: dataops (UID/GID 4500) exists on both nodes, /srv/nfs/shared on node1 is exported and mounted at /mnt/shared on node2, both directories show dataops:dataops ownership with mode 2770, and cross-node file creation preserves consistent ownership (with root correctly squashed). The independent provider-wide restart protocol was also executed thoroughly for both nodes: pre-restart healthy baselines, reboot acknowledgements, unreachability during reboot, changed boot IDs (cross-checked against the fixed after-executor lifecycle snapshots for both nodes), and full post-restart recovery of NFS export/service state, mount state, and data with a final round-trip write test. No unnecessary or lingering mutations were found; a mid-task firewall block was diagnosed and fixed with a narrowly scoped rule change, and all verification artifacts were cleaned up.\",\"limitations\":[\"cmd-46f18df72ea24287 failed with a proxy timeout mid-command (chown/chmod/mount chained together), leaving momentary ambiguity about whether the chown/chmod portion completed before the timeout; this was resolved by the subsequent successful mount and ownership verification in cmd-2818cb9a06534f16, but the exact failure point inside the chained command is not directly observable.\",\"Firewalld state on node2 (the NFS client) was not explicitly captured; this is a minor gap since inbound firewall rules on the client are not expected to block outbound NFS client traffic, but it was not directly verified.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Export /srv/nfs/shared on node1 as an NFS share","status":"satisfied","summary":"Export file /etc/exports.d/shared.exports created, nfs-server enabled/started, exportfs -v confirms /srv/nfs/shared exported to node2's IP with rw,root_squash. Export state also confirmed intact after node1 reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ceb3654ab6774d1b","cmd-b481c47f4a3a4995","cmd-28299d5bcaf64f4f"]},{"id":"req-2","requirement":"Mount the share at /mnt/shared on node2","status":"satisfied","summary":"mount output on node2 shows 10.100.251.10:/srv/nfs/shared mounted at /mnt/shared type nfs4, and fstab entry with _netdev added for persistence. Mount also confirmed recovered after node2 reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2818cb9a06534f16","cmd-e217ae63838a4da8","cmd-48c354a3f65f46f1"]},{"id":"req-3","requirement":"Shared i